{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1327942-presenting-another-werewolf-ap-storm-dragon","id":1327942,"title":"Presenting Another Werewolf AP - Storm Dragon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-28T12:27:10-07:00","id":1327942,"title":"Presenting Another Werewolf AP - Storm Dragon","content":"Hello people of the forum. It is I, viskarenvisla. I come bearing gifts.<br /> <br /> I'd like to humbly submit this game, played between myself and Mr. Shopping as per usual (the storyteller for Detroit Rock City <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/werewolf-the-forsaken-detroit-rock-city.446663/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...k-city.446663/</a> and player in The Seventh Seal <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/werewolf-the-forsaken-the-seventh-seal.775548/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...h-seal.775548/</a> which we unfortunately didn't quite finish). This game tells the tale of Kitt Dragolovitch in a sort of split-off universe, using <i>my</i> particular Werewolf canon, the same as in Seventh Seal.<br /> <br /> This game takes place in July 20XX, a few years before the events of DRC, featuring a younger, slightly less fucked up Kitt as the main character on a vengeance-mission to slay the <i>Pakhan</i> of the Bratva in America, who ordered the assassination on her father. It being WoD, she is bound to learn that the rabbit hole goes pretty damn deep<br /> <br /> Credit is given to those whose ideas have contributed but I'd like to specially mention <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar606_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"606\" data-vbnamecard=\"606\">Aynie</a> here, as someone I've been gaming with for years, who has given me a lot of interesting ideas about Werewolf and how to better make game logistics work.<br /> <br /> Anyway here's the link. I hope that those who give their time to read it enjoy it as much as I have enjoyed running it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/werewolf-the-forsaken-2e-storm-dragon.850088/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...dragon.850088/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T10:14:42-07:00","id":1328323,"title":"","content":"Hey man! I'm always excited to read what you two come up with, and am deeply tantalized with a look behind the scenes at Kitt. I wonder if this means we'll find out more about her sword, and if it is a fetish. That was always a particularly tantalizing mystery.<br /> <br /> I'm sad to hear that The Seventh Seal petered out, I was really enjoying it. Do what you have to do, though! Thanks as always for posting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T13:30:58-07:00","id":1328368,"title":"","content":"I agree with solidork, sad to hear about Seventh Seal. Thus is the curse of long games, though, and there's something to be said for a never ending story, I've always enjoyed thinking about future possibilities with them. Certainly better than a never starting one.<br /> <br /> I've been trying to read this but I'm so busy lately, I got it on my Kindle but haven't had much time for focused reading. Thoroughly interested, though, so don't take the silence as lack of interest please!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T17:06:38-07:00","id":1328406,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Seventh Seal was comfortably the best Actual Play I think I've ever read, and I'm heartbroken to hear that it ended. Still, very interested in anything new from you guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-24T10:26:48-07:00","id":1332446,"title":"","content":"Hello friends. I have posted more Storm Dragon for you to consume.<br /> <br /> It is disheartening for me to see that people are that sad about Seventh Seal's hiatus. Currently my dear colleague Shopping has a very large, serious project he's working on IRL, which understandably limits his time. Seeing as Storm Dragon just kinda materialized out of nowhere, we will run with this for a while but I'll discuss the resumption of Seventh Seal with Mr. Shopping. In truth the campaign was nearing its end...well, for that particular portion anyway.<br /> <br /> Anyway. Tune in to Storm Dragon for some lovely, violent fight-pit action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T10:35:05-07:00","id":1333850,"title":"","content":"Hail good people.<br /> <br /> I just posted a big chunk of Storm Dragon with one of the more significant fights. Enjoy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T09:53:50-07:00","id":1337331,"title":"","content":"More Storm Dragon! This time Kitt finally goes to New Orleans, but before that she tries a catfish po-boy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}